WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:24.549
Tom shook as he looked at the dragon.

2
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:29.061
"You can do this," Tom told himself.

3
00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:32.594
"You can stop the dragon!"

4
00:00:32.595 --> 00:00:35.831
Tom waved his wand.

5
00:00:35.832 --> 00:00:40.651
"Dragon—begone!" he cried.

6
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:44.996
But the dragon didn't go.

7
00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:51.068
The dragon danced.

8
00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:56.837
Tom waved his wand again and again.

9
00:00:56.838 --> 00:01:00.011
The dragon did jumping jacks.

10
00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:11.168
The dragon spun around.

11
00:01:11.169 --> 00:01:14.084
Suddenly Cat got an idea.

12
00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:17.189
She pointed to the farmer's milk cart.

13
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:26.653
"Tom, can you make the cart roll?"

14
00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:28.833
Tom waved his wand.

15
00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:32.147
"Milk cart—start!"

16
00:01:32.148 --> 00:01:37.173
The cart sat there.

17
00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:39.133
Tom tried again.

18
00:01:39.134 --> 00:01:43.080
This time the cart did move.

19
00:01:43.081 --> 00:01:47.611
It rolled fast down the hill!

20
00:01:47.612 --> 00:01:53.993
Boom! The cart crashed into a tree and flipped over.

21
00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:57.158
Milk spilled everywhere.

22
00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:01.897
Roar! The dragon roared.

23
00:02:01.898 --> 00:02:04.382
Then it froze!

24
00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:08.931
Milk was flowing toward the dragon.

25
00:02:08.932 --> 00:02:21.697
It sniffed the milk . . . and licked it up!

26
00:02:21.697 --> 00:02:24.925
The dragon roared again.

27
00:02:24.926 --> 00:02:31.746
But this time no flames came out.

28
00:02:31.747 --> 00:02:35.136
"Look!" Tom cried.

29
00:02:35.137 --> 00:02:42.693
"The dragon is leaving!"

30
00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:45.838
Tom looked at Cat.

31
00:02:45.839 --> 00:02:48.016
She shrugged.

32
00:02:48.017 --> 00:02:52.163
"The dragon was holding its belly," she said.

33
00:02:52.164 --> 00:02:58.102
"Ann said milk is good for an upset stomach."

34
00:02:58.103 --> 00:03:08.701
Everyone ran up to the roof.

35
00:03:08.702 --> 00:03:12.325
Dirk glared as the king shook Tom's hand.

36
00:03:12.326 --> 00:03:16.405
"Well done, Tom!" the king cried.

37
00:03:16.406 --> 00:03:29.543
Ann held up her roses. "Yes, Tom."
